      "code": "     WHERE assets > SOME",
      "explanation": "The SOME test is used in conjunction with one of the six SQL comparison operators (=, <>, <, <=, >, >=) to compare the test value with the results of subquery. If any of the individual comparisons yield a TRUE result, the SOME test results a TRUE results. SOME and ANY are equivalent. In this example, asset of every branch is compared with every assets of branch in 'Brooklyn'."
